## PART E: DEBUGGING AND CODE CORRECTION

### E1. Grade Function

A grade function should check the highest mark ranges first.

Correct logic:

```dart
if (mark >= 80) {
  return 'A';
} else if (mark >= 70) {
  return 'B';
} else if (mark >= 50) {
  return 'C';
} else {
  return 'F';
}
```

**Explanation:** Checking lower ranges first can cause higher marks to receive incorrect grades.

### E2. Palindrome Function

A palindrome reads the same forward and backward.

A corrected function is:

```dart
bool isPalindrome(String word) {
  int i = 0;

  while (i < word.length ~/ 2) {
    if (word[i] != word[word.length - 1 - i]) {
      return false;
    }
    i++;
  }

  return true;
}
```

**Explanation:** The correct last-character index is `word.length - 1`. The original incorrect index can cause a RangeError. This version is case-sensitive.

